                {
                  "resource_id": "levelled_description",
                  "stats": {
                    "id": "levelled_description_1971fd2a4a88",
                    "level": {
                      "value": 7
                    },
                    "description": {
                      "value": "All communication is filled with slight tells and signals. If you interact with someone for at least 10 minutes, their regional words, pronunciation changes, and nonverbal cues provide you with a minor fact about their social environment, such as their hometown or certain groups they might belong to. If a target of this ability is being deceptive about their social environment, such as a commoner pretending to be a noble, they must attempt a Deception, Society, or appropriate Lore check against your Society DC, providing you a false minor fact consistent with their assumed identity on a success.\n\nOnce you've gleaned one or more true minor facts about a person, you can then incorporate these mannerisms into your speech to present yourself in a way that they find familiar. This grants you a +1 circumstance bonus to your Diplomacy and Deception checks with them."
                    }
                  }
                }
              ]
            },
